 "hold_blocks": {
  "how": "AHD's hold, in samples from the sample the attack reaches full scale: HOLD 0 holds 2 (ATK 10, DEC 35: the DSP's level in that block falls 9 samples, not 11; the fall ratio and the attack measured as above); 127: until the note-off (record 63's default). 1..126 (2026-11-18, scripts/measure_amp_hold.py search): the DSP counts the samples held (its word 0x2547c4, 32 a block) and falls when the count reaches the knob's length; each knob's length found by starting every block in the hold at full scale with that count poked to a trial value (a binary search), the block's fall (n samples at DEC 35's known ratio) giving it to the sample. Checked against plain runs: HOLD 1 14, 2 40, 3 82, 4 144, 16 3085 (the level's first fall). Some neighbours hold the same (8 and 9, 12 and 13, 17 and 18, 25 and 26, 35 and 36, 51 and 52, 71 and 72, 103 and 104), as the DSP has them. HOLD 126: 470,679 samples (9.8 s). The DSP's memory holds no table of the measured attack steps (searched: L1, L2, DDR).",
